# Cloudflare Pages reads this file to attach HTTP response headers per path.
# Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, followed by indented `Header-Name: value`
# lines that apply to every response matching it. Docs:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This file is NOT covered by `npm run build` or any test in this repo. A wrong
# value here does not fail CI — it fails silently in the browser: the disallowed
# script/style/font/request is just dropped, and the only trace is a
# Content-Security-Policy violation line in the DevTools console. Verify any
# change here against a real deployed preview and check the console, not just
# by re-running the test suite.
#
# connect-src includes `https:` and `http://localhost:*` because the AI
# provider base URL (Admin > AI settings, openai-compatible path) is a
# user-supplied runtime value — it can be any cloud endpoint or a local
# Ollama/vLLM instance — so it cannot be pinned to a fixed origin list here.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://openapi.twse.com.tw https://www.tpex.org.tw https: http://localhost:*; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
